# Thymeleaf Layout Dialect

When creating or editing full-page Thymeleaf templates, use **Thymeleaf Layout Dialect** instead of repeating GNB/LNB/footer/scripts in every file.

Reference pilot: `admin/news/detail.html` + `layouts/admin.html`.

## Layout files

| File | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `layouts/admin.html` | 관리자 화면 (GNB + LNB + admin shell) |
| `layouts/auth.html` | 관리자 로그인 (auth shell, GNB/LNB 없음) |
| `layouts/public.html` | (추후) 사용자 공개 화면 |

- Shell markup lives in `layouts/*.html` only.
- Reusable partials stay in `fragments/layout.html` (`head`, `gnb`, `lnb`, `breadcrumb`, `footer`, `scripts`).
- Do **not** duplicate `th:replace` for gnb/lnb/footer/scripts in pages that use a layout.

## Page template pattern

Every new or migrated page must declare the layout decorator and put **page body only** in `layout:fragment="content"`.

```html
<!-- screen: … / purpose: … / created: yyyy-mm-dd -->
<html lang="ko"
      xmlns:th="http://www.thymeleaf.org"
      xmlns:layout="http://www.ultraq.net.nz/thymeleaf/layout"
      layout:decorate="~{layouts/admin}">
<head>
    <title layout:fragment="title">화면 제목</title>
</head>
<body>
<th:block layout:fragment="content">

    <!-- 브레드크럼 시작 -->
    ...
    <!-- 하단 버튼 끝 -->

</th:block>
</body>
</html>
```

## Controller model (admin layout)

- GNB/LNB active state comes from `adminNavigation` (`COAdminNavigationAdvice`) — do **not** set `layoutGnbActive` / `layoutLnbActive` per controller.
- Set the page `<title layout:fragment="title">` in the template. Use `th:text` when the title is dynamic.

```html
<title th:text="${survey?.surveySeq} != null ? '설문 상세' : '설문 등록'">설문 상세</title>
```

## Optional layout fragments

| Fragment | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `content` | **Required.** Main page body inside `<main class="admin-content">` |
| `pageScripts` | Page-only `<script>` tags after common scripts |
| `pageExtras` | Modal markup etc. between admin shell and footer |
| `pageComment` | Optional screen-purpose HTML comment at body start |

## Layout-side fragment placement (critical)

Pages use `<th:block layout:fragment="content">`, which **replaces** the matching layout node including its tag. Never put `layout:fragment="content"` on `<main class="admin-content">` in the layout — that drops the wrapper and scatters page nodes as direct children of `.admin-shell`, breaking the CSS grid.

```html
<!-- layouts/admin.html — correct -->
<main class="admin-content">
    <th:block layout:fragment="content"></th:block>
</main>
```

```html
<!-- wrong — th:block on the page replaces <main> entirely -->
<main class="admin-content" layout:fragment="content"></main>
```

## Legacy pages

- All admin templates under `templates/admin/` use Layout Dialect.
- Client templates still use inline shell until migrated separately.

## With markup rules

- Inside `layout:fragment="content"`, follow `html-markup-layout.mdc` (element line breaks, block region comments, blank lines between regions).

## Do not

- Add Apache Tiles or duplicate full HTML shell in every page.
- Put gnb/footer/scripts in page templates that already use `layouts/admin.html`.
- Omit `layout:decorate` on a page that only defines `layout:fragment="content"` (shell will not render).
